@using GameTownApp.Services
@inject LanCountState Counts
@implements IDisposable

@*
    The sidebar's LAN suggestions entry, shown only when the integration is set up.

    Most installs will never connect a LAN bot, and a permanent link to a screen that can only say
    "nothing here" reads as an unfinished chore — the same reasoning as RelinkNavLink. Unlike that
    one, this link stays once the integration exists even when the wishlist is empty: re-linking is a
    one-time migration chore that genuinely finishes, whereas suggestions keep arriving and the
    "Linked" and "Set aside" tabs are worth reaching between LANs. The count is a badge rather than
    the condition.

    A COMPONENT rather than a few lines in NavMenu, so it sits inside the Contribute branch of
    AuthorizeView and is never instantiated until authorization has resolved — an anonymous visitor
    must not fire a request that comes back 401. The route itself is untouched: /lan-suggestions
    still loads if it is typed or bookmarked.

    THE COUNT COMES FROM LanCountState, not from a read of its own, and that is the fix for two
    separate faults:

      * It used to read once in OnInitializedAsync and never again, so setting a suggestion aside
        moved the tab badge on the LAN screen from 79 to 78 while this went on saying 79 until a full
        page reload. Neither number was wrong when it was fetched, which is what made it hard to
        notice and easy to distrust.

      * It used to decide whether to render by calling Get("all") — the ENTIRE suggestion list —
        whenever the unmatched count was zero. An empty wishlist is the healthy steady state, so the
        common case downloaded every suggestion in the database on every page load of the app, to
        answer one boolean. The count endpoint now returns a total alongside the unmatched figure.
*@

@if (Counts.Total > 0)
{
    <NavLink class="gt-nav__link" href="lan-suggestions">
        <span class="bi bi-discord" aria-hidden="true"></span> LAN suggestions
        @if (Counts.Unmatched > 0)
        {
            <span class="badge bg-secondary ms-1">@Counts.Unmatched</span>
        }
    </NavLink>
}

@code {
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        Counts.Changed += OnChanged;

        // Already read by whatever got here first — usually this component, occasionally the LAN
        // screen on a deep link. Either way there is no reason to ask twice.
        if (!Counts.Loaded) await Counts.Refresh();
    }

    // Nothing renders on a failure: the state swallows it. This link is an offer, not a control
    // anyone is waiting on, and an error in the sidebar would be louder than the link it replaced.
    private void OnChanged() => StateHasChanged();

    public void Dispose() => Counts.Changed -= OnChanged;
}
